### What I played (headless Chromium via Playwright 1.64, file:// open, 1366x768)

Scripts and captures are in `acceptance/build-1/` (`play.py`, `deaths.py`, `log.json`, `p*.png`).

| Req | Observed | Verdict |
|---|---|---|
| R1 | Opens from `index.html` over file:// and loads its assets; no console or page errors | met |
| R2 | 20x20 grid inside a wall ring; one cell per 120 ms tick; keeps moving without input (wall hit after about 1.2 s from the start) | met |
| R3 | Arrows steer; a reverse press is ignored and play continues; 3 turns queued in one tick are all applied; `scrollY` stays 0 | met |
| R4 | 6 foods in a row: each gave exactly +1 length and +1 score; the HUD matched the state at once; food is drawn from free cells only (code `spawnFood`) | met |
| R5 | Wall: game over, "You ran into the wall." Self: game over, "You ran into yourself." (game 1, `p3`). The tail-cell rule is in the code (`bodyLen`) | met |
| R6 | Title: SNAKE logo, arrow-key help, Start button, Enter/Space hint (`p1`) | met |
| R7 | "Score N" above the board during play, plus Best (`p2`) | met |
| R8 | Game over: cause, final score, Play again button and Enter/Space hint. Play again by click and by Enter gives score 0, length 3, playing | met |
| R9 | Neon-on-dark is consistent and legible; the page is 768 px high in a 768 px viewport, so no scrolling | met |

Minor, not blocking: dev material (`checks/`) ships inside the delivery; it does no harm to play.

### Playtest (world/playtester#2, answered and closed)
playtester played release build-1 (playtester `daa23709398b844c2f580793a12c434249e20bce`: `reports/build-1.md`, `evidence/build-1/` screenshots and `full-session.webm`). They found no defect against R1–R9. Each food gave +1 length and +1 point, both deaths showed a clear cause, and play again worked three times in a row (Enter, click, Space). The game fits 1366x657, 1280x600 and 1024x600. Their notes, which I do not count as failures:
- An arrow key does not start the game from the title. Not required: R6 asks for the title to say how to start, and it does (Enter/Space/Start button).
- The board is heavily dimmed behind the overlays. The overlay text stays legible, so R9 holds.
- Audio quality was unheard (headless). Sound is optional per the brief, and the files load without errors.

### QA (world/qa#3, answered and closed)
qa at `fd83a060886f0b279a430fd743b9ae933dee28f1` ran 27 independent checks (`qa/check.py`, `qa/report-build-1.json`) and all 27 pass. Highlights: a 60-point bot game checked every frame (length 3+score, food never on the snake, HUD equal to the state); the tail-cell rule; play again three times; no scroll at six viewports.
- Finding: the grid lines are nearly invisible (tile edges about 1.1:1 against the fill). My brief's R2 asks for a *visible* grid. I confirmed it in my own `p2-play.png`, where the cells are only just perceptible.
- Not defects: Best updates only at game over (it is not a requirement); an arrow key does not start the game (Enter/Space/button is accepted).

### Decision
`revise` to artist in world/artist#5: raise the cell-edge contrast in `assets/img/tile.png` (same size and name). I told game-developer in world/game-developer#4 not to add a code overlay as well. Next: re-check the new assembly, publish build-2, have playtester re-play it, then approve.

