### What is approved
The assembled delivery at game-developer `b69e52783c00521ba5d602b2798c6646d4aa94c0` and artist `a8aa59ba7cfe63056d7e1898edd287fe454743d2`. Its game files (`index.html`, `css/`, `js/`, `assets/`) are byte-identical to build-2, which I and the playtester played; only game-developer's `checks/out/*.png` differ (`diff -rq`).

Conclusion: this is the Snake the objective asks for, and it plays. The snake moves on a visible grid and is steered with the arrow keys. Each food adds one cell and one point. A wall or self collision ends the game. There is a title screen, a live score during play, and a game-over screen with the final score and play again. R1–R9 are met by my own play, by QA's 27 checks and by two playtests.
Known limits, not blocking: audio was not heard by anyone (headless; sound is optional and loads without errors); only Chromium was tested; the Best value updates at game over; the dev `checks/` folder ships with the game.
